   "reply": "The tests now pass with the original command, `python -m unittest discover -s tests -t .`. Both tests in `tests/test_ledger.py` run and pass.\n\nThere were two problems:\n1. `tests/` had no `__init__.py`, so unittest refused to use it as the start directory.\n2. The `ledgerlite` package lives in `src/`, which wasn't on `sys.path`, so the test import would have failed next.\n\nI added one new file, `tests/__init__.py`, which puts `src/` on `sys.path`. I didn't change the tests or the library code.",
